  "citations": [
    {
      "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
      "quote": "(4) The time allowed for doing a relevant act may be extended, whether before or after that time has expired."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part17/1#1",
      "quote": "If a trade mark application has lapsed prior to acceptance, an extension of time for acceptance will need to be filed. This extension will need to be approved before a deferment request can be processed."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part16/1/1/2",
      "quote": "If this is done before the prescribed period expires (see paragraph 1.4) and during the first six months after the initial 15 months, it may be done simply by way of a written request, accompanied by the appropriate fee."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
      "quote": "(2) If, because of: (a) an error or omission by the person concerned or by his or her agent; or (b) circumstances beyond the control of the person concerned; a relevant act that is required by this Act to be done within a certain time is not, or cannot be, done within that time, the Registrar may, on application made by the person concerned in accordance with the regulations, extend the time for doing the act. (3) If: (a) a relevant act that a person is required by this Act to do within a certain time is not, or cannot be, done within that time; and (b) on application made by that person in accordance with the regulations, the Registrar is of the opinion that special circumstances exist that justify an extension of that time; the Registrar may extend the time for doing the act."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part16/1/1/3",
      "quote": "After 21 months, the application may only be extended under the provisions of section 224. Except for extensions granted because of the Registrar’s error or omission, the particular provisions require, in addition to a written request in an approved form, (and the appropriate fee) a declaration setting out the facts upon which the grounds specified in the application for an extension of time are based (regulation 21.25). This declaration will be considered by the Registrar, who has the discretion not to extend the time, if he or she does not consider the reasons for the application for an extension of time to be sufficient."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMA1995/s224",
      "quote": "(1) The Registrar must extend the time for doing a relevant act that is required by this Act to be done within a certain time if the act is not, or cannot be, done within that time because of an error or omission by: (a) the Registrar or a Deputy Registrar; or (b) an employee; or (c) a person providing, or proposing to provide, services for the benefit of the Trade Marks Office."
    }
  ],
  "answer": "**You can seek an extension after the deadline has expired.** Section 224(4) of the Act expressly permits this; it does not guarantee that an extension will be granted. [TMA1995/s224]\n\n1. **File an extension-of-time request for acceptance.** Manual practice says that, if the application has already lapsed before acceptance, that extension must be filed and approved before a deferment request can be processed. Deferment is therefore not a substitute for obtaining the extension in that situation. [TMM/Part17/1#1]\n\n2. **Explain the applicable ground.** Under the Act, the Registrar may extend time where the missed deadline resulted from your or your agent’s error or omission, or circumstances beyond your control (s 224(2)). The Registrar may also extend time where special circumstances justify it (s 224(3)). Where the specified Office-side error or omission caused the failure, s 224(1) requires an extension. [TMA1995/s224]\n\n3. **Provide the request, fee and supporting declaration.** The Manual’s section 224 guidance specifies a written request in an approved form, the appropriate fee and a declaration setting out the facts supporting the grounds, except for extensions because of the Registrar’s error or omission. It also says that, after 21 months, extension is available only under section 224. [TMM/Part16/1/1/3]\n\n**Do not assume the simpler “easy” extension procedure applies after a missed deadline:** the supplied Manual passage makes that procedure conditional on requesting it before the prescribed period expires and within the stated six-month window. [TMM/Part16/1/1/2]\n\nThe supplied passages do not identify the actual form, fee amount or lodgement channel. No outcome for your application can be determined from them."
